<title>LEBANON: Lebanon issues January-November debt figures.</title>
<headline>Lebanon issues January-November debt figures.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's finance ministry issued the following public debt figures to end of November (in millions of dollars unless otherwise stated).</p>
<p>	   Net Domestic     Net Domestic     Foreign debt   total</p>
<p>	  Debt (LBP blns)	 Debt</p>
<p>    Jan   9,614		   6,041	  1,305	    7,346</p>
<p>    Feb  10,032		   6,317	  1,333	    7,650</p>
<p>    Mar  10,238		   6,465	  1,360	    7,828</p>
<p>    Apr  10,668		   6,752	  1,394	    8,146</p>
<p>    May  10,939		   6,945	  1,526	    8,471</p>
<p>    Jun  11,236		   7,152	  1,579	    8,731</p>
<p>    Jul  11,676		   7,454	  1,574	    9,028</p>
<p>    Aug  11,961		   7,657	  1,605	    9,262</p>
<p>    Sep  12,434		   7,978	  1,666	    9,644</p>
<p>    Oct  12,733		   8,183	  1,657	    9,840</p>
<p>    Nov  12,965		   8,343	  1,677	    10,020</p>
<p>($1 = 1,554 Lebanese pounds at end of November)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 353078 645456 602057</p>
</text>
